<title>USA: ECC Q3 shr loss $0.24 vs loss $0.05.</title>
<headline>ECC Q3 shr loss $0.24 vs loss $0.05.</headline>
<dateline>WAYNE, Pa. 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands except share and per share data)</p>
<p>	     3 Months	3 Months	 9 Months   9 Months</p>
<p>		Ended	   Ended	    Ended	Ended</p>
<p>	     3/31/97	 3/31/96	  3/31/97    3/31/96</p>
<p>Net Sales  $15,757	 $27,305	  $63,796     $85,976</p>
<p>Gross</p>
<p> Profit	  977	   3,488	    8,193	16,252</p>
<p>Total</p>
<p>  Expenses   3,492	   3,892	   11,366	10,839</p>
<p>Operating (Loss)</p>
<p> /Income    (2,515)	   (404)	  (3,173)	5,413</p>
<p>Net (Loss)</p>
<p> /Income    $(1,952)	  $(398)	 $(3,386)     $2,848</p>
<p>(Loss)/Earnings Per</p>
<p>Common Share and</p>
<p>Common Share</p>
<p> Equivalents $(0.24)	$(0.05)	  $(0.42)	$0.36</p>
<p>Weighted Average Number</p>
<p>of Common and Common</p>
<p>Share Equivalents</p>
<p> Outstanding 8,033,389   7,777,082	8,021,577   7,908,764</p>
<p>NOTE: Company said the fiscal third quarter loss was due to increased overhead costs domestically arising from sharply reduced revenues and termination costs related to staff reduction, higher than projected costs to complete two major domestic contracts, one of which was finished in May, 1997 while the other is scheduled for completion in June, 1997. The domestic simulation business incurred a loss in the quarter, but continued to be profitable on a year-to-date basis.</p>
<p>Full company name is ECC International Corp.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
